<% content_for :title, "AWSM Privacy" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "public-site" %>
<%= render "shared/public_header" %>
<main class="site-container trust-page">
  <header class="trust-page__header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Factual product explanation · not a legal policy</p>
    <h1>What stays local. What a server can see.</h1>
    <p>This page describes AWSM's current technical behavior. An operator of a self-hosted server controls that deployment and its logs.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose-stack">
    <section><h2>Local Capture and Vault content</h2><p>Captured page content, local projections, decryption keys, and the Recovery Phrase belong to the client environment. A local-only Vault does not require an Account or Coordination Server.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Derived local views</h2><p>Clients may create encrypted, rebuildable local materializations from Vault content. They are not opaque Host items. AWSM does not currently ship a user-facing AI feature or a remote embedding-provider integration.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Account and session records</h2><p>A Coordination Server stores a private Account username, a password digest, browser and API session records, and Host-local access and quota records for Hosted Replicas. AWSM does not collect an Account email address. The Account password is received by the server for authentication; it is not a Vault decryption password.</p><p>After browser signup or sign-in, AWSM also sets <code>awsm_browser_session_hint</code>, a first-party functional cookie containing only a random opaque value. It is readable by this site's JavaScript so anonymous visitors do not need an Account-status request. It contains no credential or Account data and cannot authenticate you.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Synchronization data</h2><p>A Replica Host stores opaque encrypted item bytes. It also sees Host-local identifiers, byte counts, request timing, traffic patterns, and IP or access logs. It cannot decrypt the items or establish the Vault identities they represent.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Public website</h2><p>The AWSM landing and public trust pages include no analytics, tracking pixels, marketing cookies, third-party scripts, or remote fonts. Their shared anonymous response may be cached by the deployment's CDN. The CDN and ordinary server access logs may still receive standard connection and request metadata. Account, signup, and session responses are not shared-cache content.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Deletion boundaries</h2><p>Removing local data affects that Client installation; it cannot erase items already held by another Replica or retained under a Host's documented deletion process. AWSM does not promise remote wipe.</p></section>
  </div>
</main>
<%= render "shared/public_footer" %>
